  "name": "Anushka Chkheidze",
  "editorial_article": "Anushka Chkheidze is a Georgian electronic composer, producer, and performer whose work has become a defining voice in the contemporary Tbilisi electronic scene. Emerging from the vibrant and experimental landscape of the Georgian capital, Chkheidze creates music that defies easy categorization, weaving together elements of IDM, ambient, and electroacoustic composition. Her sonic palette is characterized by a delicate balance of tranquil, minimalist synthesizer layers and complex, often glitch-influenced rhythmic structures. This interplay creates an immersive, atmospheric quality that often evokes themes of alienation and introspection.\n\nSince her entry into the international spotlight, Chkheidze has been recognized for her unique sensibility and technical precision. She has released significant projects on labels such as CES Records, where her output demonstrates a deep commitment to exploring both the synthetic and organic textures of sound. Her live performances—documented at major European festivals and platforms like Eurosonic Noorderslag—are renowned for their immersive, world-building nature, often featuring evolving soundscapes that challenge the listener's expectations of both pop and experimental music. As a pivotal figure in the current wave of Caucasian electronic artists, she continues to push the boundaries of her craft, bridging the gap between academic electroacoustic approaches and accessible electronic music aesthetics.",
